version: 2
title: Claude configuration dimensions
description: Where a piece of Claude configuration lives, who owns it, what it is, and when it loads. Answer the questions to see what exists in that cell; the briefs beside this book explain each group.
decisions:
  - key: harness
    label: Where does Claude run?
    detail: The outermost axis. It decides which of the other questions apply at all.
    values:
      - key: chat
        label: Chat app
        detail: claude.ai on the web or in the desktop app, including what Cowork did before the merge
        activates: [anchor]
      - key: code
        label: Claude Code
        detail: The same engine in the terminal, the desktop app's Code tab, an IDE extension or a cloud session
        activates: [host]
  - key: anchor
    label: What is the chat anchored to?
    detail: Picked when the chat starts. It decides what reach means here.
    values:
      - key: none
        label: Nothing
        detail: Account-wide sources only
      - key: project
        label: A Project
        detail: Its instructions, knowledge files and memory space come along
      - key: folder
        label: A folder
        detail: File access to the folder; whether its CLAUDE.md is read is still to verify
  - key: host
    label: Which host runs Claude Code?
    detail: The host changes the tools on offer, not where instructions come from, except in the cloud.
    values:
      - key: terminal
        label: Terminal
      - key: desktop
        label: Desktop app, Code tab
      - key: ide
        label: VS Code or JetBrains extension
      - key: cloud
        label: Cloud session
        detail: Another machine. Only the repo's own files travel there
  - key: owner
    label: Who owns it?
    detail: Who writes it and who sees it.
    values:
      - key: org
        label: Org
        detail: Deployed by an admin
      - key: team
        label: Team
        detail: Committed in the repo, or a Project shared with people
      - key: me
        label: Me
        detail: My home folder, a git-ignored local file, or my own account
  - key: reach
    label: Where does it apply?
    values:
      - key: everywhere
        label: Everywhere
        detail: Every project on this machine, or the whole account
      - key: tree
        label: A folder and everything below it
        activates: [tree-level]
      - key: project
        label: One Project
        when: [harness=chat]
  - key: tree-level
    label: Which folder?
    values:
      - key: ancestor
        label: An ancestor folder
        detail: Its CLAUDE.md applies to every repo below it
      - key: root
        label: The repo root
      - key: subfolder
        label: A subfolder
        detail: Its CLAUDE.md loads when Claude works on files inside it
      - key: pattern
        label: Files matching a path pattern
        detail: A rule with a paths list in its frontmatter
  - key: kind
    label: What kind of thing is it?
    values:
      - key: instruction
        label: Instruction
        detail: Standing guidance on how to behave
        activates: [instruction-place]
      - key: rule
        label: Rule
        detail: An instruction in its own file, optionally path-scoped. Claude Code only
        activates: [rule-scope]
      - key: skill
        label: Skill
        detail: A procedure for one kind of task, with its scripts and references
        activates: [skill-source]
      - key: memory
        label: Memory
        detail: What Claude wrote down from earlier sessions
        activates: [memory-regime, memory-gate]
      - key: knowledge
        label: Knowledge files
        detail: Reference material to consult, not guidance
      - key: settings
        label: Settings
        detail: Permissions, hooks, environment. Enforced by the harness, never read as text
        activates: [settings-tier]
  - key: instruction-place
    label: Where does the instruction sit?
    values:
      - key: user-claudemd
        label: '~\.claude\CLAUDE.md'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: ancestor-claudemd
        label: An ancestor folder's CLAUDE.md
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: root-claudemd
        label: The repo's CLAUDE.md
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: dot-claudemd
        label: '.claude\CLAUDE.md'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: local-claudemd
        label: CLAUDE.local.md
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: subfolder-claudemd
        label: A subfolder's CLAUDE.md
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: import
        label: A file pulled in by an @import line
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: settings-general
        label: 'Settings > General'
        when: [harness=chat]
      - key: project-instructions
        label: A Project's instructions field
        when: [harness=chat]
      - key: folder-claudemd
        label: The anchored folder's CLAUDE.md
        detail: Still to verify after the merge
        when: [harness=chat]
  - key: rule-scope
    label: Is the rule scoped to paths?
    values:
      - key: unscoped
        label: Unscoped
        detail: Loads at start like an extra CLAUDE.md
      - key: scoped
        label: Path-scoped
        detail: A paths list in its frontmatter. Loads when a matching file is touched
  - key: skill-source
    label: Where does the skill come from?
    values:
      - key: user-skills
        label: '~\.claude\skills'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: project-skills
        label: '.claude\skills'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: plugin
        label: A plugin
      - key: synced
        label: Synced down from claude.ai
        detail: '~\.claude\skills\synced'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: uploaded
        label: 'Settings > Skills'
        detail: Uploaded by me, or provisioned by the org
        when: [harness=chat]
  - key: memory-regime
    label: How is memory kept?
    values:
      - key: auto
        label: Auto-memory on
        detail: '~\.claude\projects\<key>\memory, machine-local, per repository'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: relocated
        label: Auto-memory relocated
        detail: autoMemoryDirectory in a settings file
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: brief
        label: Auto-memory off, a memory brief
        detail: A curated brief in the repo, injected by a hook. The orchestration regime
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: account
        label: Account memory
        detail: 'Settings > Memory, with a space per Project'
        when: [harness=chat]
      - key: app-db
        label: The app's per-folder memory
        detail: Kept in the desktop app's database. Still to verify after the merge
        when: [harness=chat]
  - key: memory-gate
    label: Who decides what is written?
    values:
      - key: claude
        label: Claude writes on its own
      - key: ask
        label: Shown first, written only on a yes
        detail: A rule or a playbook event. Followed, not enforced
      - key: enforced
        label: A hook or permission rule refuses the write
  - key: settings-tier
    label: Which settings tier?
    values:
      - key: managed
        label: Managed
        detail: managed-settings.json, deployed by the org
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: user
        label: User
        detail: '~\.claude\settings.json, me in every project'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: project
        label: Shared project
        detail: '.claude\settings.json, everyone in the repo'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: project-local
        label: Project local
        detail: '.claude\settings.local.json, me in this repo'
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: cli
        label: Command line
        detail: claude --settings, this session only
        when: [harness=code]
      - key: account
        label: Account settings
        detail: The Settings pages of claude.ai
        when: [harness=chat]
  - key: load
    label: When does it enter context?
    values:
      - key: start
        label: At session start
        detail: Whole file, every session
      - key: path
        label: When a matching path is touched
        detail: A path-scoped rule, a subfolder's CLAUDE.md
      - key: invoke
        label: When invoked
        detail: A skill body, by /name or by Claude's choice
      - key: open
        label: When Claude opens it
        detail: A memory topic file, a knowledge file, any file in the folder
      - key: hook
        label: Injected by a hook at an event
        detail: SessionStart, or every prompt
      - key: retrieval
        label: Found by search when the question matches
        detail: Large Project knowledge
  - key: binding
    label: How does it bind?
    values:
      - key: context
        label: Read as context
        detail: Followed by judgment. The more specific, the more consistently
      - key: enforced
        label: Enforced by the harness
        detail: A hook, a permission rule, a setting
events:
  - key: where
    label: Where it runs
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Where it runs
    detail: Explained in where-it-runs.brief beside this book.
    hint: Answer where Claude runs to see what that harness reads.
    content:
      key: where
      label: What this harness reads
      kind: md
      by: [harness]
      docs:
        harness=chat: |
          The chat app reads from the account first: Settings > General for standing instructions, Settings > Memory, Settings > Skills, and the connectors you enabled. Anchoring the chat to a Project or a folder adds that anchor's sources on top.

          Nothing on this PC is read unless the chat is anchored to a folder. The one thing that reaches disk from the account is the skills, synced down for Claude Code.
        harness=code: |
          Claude Code reads files: the CLAUDE.md chain from the home folder down through every ancestor to the working directory, the rules folders, the skills folders, the settings tiers and the auto-memory index. Everything loads from disk at session start, and the same set loads in every host.

          What the host changes is the tool set. The cloud is the exception, where only the repo's own files exist.
  - key: host-changes
    label: What the host changes
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Where it runs
    detail: Explained in where-it-runs.brief beside this book.
    when: [harness=code]
    hint: Answer which host to see what it adds.
    content:
      key: host-changes
      label: What this host adds
      kind: md
      by: [host]
      docs:
        host=terminal: |
          The plain CLI. The files above, the built-in tools, and the MCP servers named in the settings tiers and .mcp.json. Nothing app-specific.

          `/context` shows which CLAUDE.md, rules and memory loaded in this session. `/memory` opens them.
        host=desktop: |
          The same files, plus the desktop app's own servers: a browser pane, a terminal pane, session and sidebar controls, and the skills synced from claude.ai shown as one group.

          Probe sessions run from the terminal and from this Code tab saw the same eleven tokens, so the host does not change the sources.
        host=ide: |
          The same files, plus the editor's context: diagnostics, the current selection, and diffs shown in the editor.
        host=cloud: |
          Runs on another machine. The repo's committed files travel: its CLAUDE.md, .claude\rules, .claude\skills and .claude\settings.json.

          Nothing from ~\.claude on this PC does: no user CLAUDE.md, no user rules, no user skills, no auto-memory.
  - key: anchor-brings
    label: What the anchor brings
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Where it runs
    detail: Explained in where-it-runs.brief beside this book.
    when: [harness=chat]
    hint: Answer what the chat is anchored to.
    content:
      key: anchor-brings
      label: What this anchor adds
      kind: md
      by: [anchor]
      docs:
        anchor=none: |
          Account-wide sources only: Settings > General, Settings > Memory, Settings > Skills, connectors.

          Expected probe result: only the account-level tokens.
        anchor=project: |
          The account sources plus the Project's instructions field, its knowledge files, small totals whole and large totals by search, and the Project's own memory space.

          Expected probe result: the Project's token and nothing from disk.
        anchor=folder: |
          The account sources plus file access to the folder.

          Three open tests: whether the folder's CLAUDE.md is read, whether the old per-folder instructions field survived the merge, and whether a memory saved here lands in the account or stays on this PC.
  - key: cell
    label: What exists in this cell
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Owner and reach
    detail: Explained in owner-and-reach.brief beside this book.
    hint: Answer who owns it and where it applies to see the mechanisms in that cell.
    content:
      key: cell
      label: The mechanisms here
      kind: md
      by: [owner, reach]
      docs:
        owner=org,reach=everywhere: |
          A managed CLAUDE.md and managed-settings.json deployed by an admin, plus skills provisioned through managed plugins or Settings > Skills.

          Empty on this PC.
        owner=org,reach=tree: |
          No mechanism. An org reaches a single folder only through what the team commits there.
        owner=org,reach=project: |
          No separate mechanism. A Project shared with the whole organisation is the team cell.
        owner=team,reach=everywhere: |
          No mechanism. Nothing a team writes applies to every repo on a machine. That is the org's cell, or a plugin marketplace.
        owner=team,reach=tree: |
          The most populated cell: CLAUDE.md at an ancestor folder, the repo root, .claude\CLAUDE.md or a subfolder; .claude\rules; .claude\skills; .claude\settings.json; .mcp.json.

          All committed, so everyone who clones the repo gets them.
        owner=team,reach=project: |
          A claude.ai Project shared with people: its instructions, knowledge files and memory space.
        owner=me,reach=everywhere: |
          ~\.claude\CLAUDE.md, ~\.claude\rules, ~\.claude\skills, ~\.claude\settings.json, ~\.claude\agents.

          In the chat app: Settings > General, Settings > Memory and Settings > Skills.
        owner=me,reach=tree: |
          CLAUDE.local.md, .claude\settings.local.json, and auto-memory under ~\.claude\projects\<key>\memory.

          No personal rules or skills exist for a single repo.
        owner=me,reach=project: |
          A private Project: its instructions, knowledge files and memory space, seen by me alone.
  - key: kind-loads
    label: How this kind loads and binds
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Kinds
    detail: Explained in kinds.brief and loading.brief beside this book.
    hint: Answer what kind of thing it is.
    content:
      key: kind-loads
      label: Load and binding for this kind
      kind: md
      by: [kind]
      docs:
        kind=instruction: |
          Loads at start, whole file, every session. A subfolder's CLAUDE.md waits until Claude works there. Read as context.

          Claude Code loads a CLAUDE.md of up to 4 MiB and skips a larger one. Shorter files are followed more consistently.
        kind=rule: |
          Same as an instruction, one file per topic. Unscoped, it loads at start. With a paths list, it waits for a matching file. Read as context. Claude Code only.
        kind=skill: |
          Two stages. The frontmatter description loads at start, so Claude knows when to reach for it. The body and its files load when invoked.

          Costs almost nothing until used. Read as context.
        kind=memory: |
          The MEMORY.md index loads at start, the first 200 lines or 25KB. Topic files load when Claude opens them.

          A memory brief loads through a hook instead: an outline at SessionStart, the area on demand. Read as context. The write side is where enforcement can sit.
        kind=knowledge: |
          Small totals load whole at chat start. Large totals load by search, only the passages that match the question.

          In Claude Code the folder's files are read on demand. Reference, never guidance.
        kind=settings: |
          Read by the harness, never by Claude: permissions, hooks, environment, feature toggles. Enforced.

          A hook is the one setting that puts text into context, at the event it is wired to.
